# Line endings
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contributors work on Windows, macOS and Linux. Without this file, Git's
# core.autocrlf setting decides line endings per machine, so the same edit can
# arrive as a whole-file diff simply because someone else's checkout used CRLF.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect which files are text; `eol=lf` stores AND checks
# them out with LF everywhere. Every file in this repository is text, so one
# rule covers it.
#
# Note for the first commit after adding this file: Git may renormalise
# existing files, which can show up as changes to files nobody edited. That is
# expected and happens once.
* text=auto eol=lf
